{
  "dom_id": "step-e14197",
  "name": "Example: Dividing a Whole Number by a Non-Unit Fraction",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/45d4e4ca4f1cdfddcb624dccf32cb053818a2fd70cbb7b5a02d1ff30f9784e2b.png)\n\n \n\nThe model above represents $3$ wholes. Use the model to determine the missing number in the following division problem. \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/3cc63b591954621f88580b0cfbfd27c455f9457304184410e94060c446f4d11e.svg)",
  "worked_solution": "We proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we split each whole into fifths.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/9c10c283125b23a553855e247149fba126c1977bf62a487b09121eb539dabfbf.png)\n\n \n\n- Next, we create groups of ${\\color{red}{\\dfrac3{5}}}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/a8ee616adc072552e64182bba65bd74754b4a16857bfc7fe7e411ab9784bd331.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, we count the groups.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/ad9c3bcb60e6277ae536b00489b3f4267a31fb9f2d0a7af368ee0cc43215287d.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $\\color{blue}3$ wholes into groups of ${\\color{red}{\\dfrac3{5}}},$ we get ${\\color{purple}{5}}$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\div \\dfrac{3}{{5}} = \\fbox{5}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the missing number is $\\bbox[3pt, Gainsboro]{\\color{purple}5}.$",
